# .cursorrules — INSTRUCTOR REFERENCE SOLUTION
# Completed version of the Module 2/3/1b exercises. Use to check trainee
# submissions or to unblock a stuck group — do not distribute up front.

## Project Context
This is a small Retail/CPG-style analytics service: it ingests sales data,
produces baseline demand forecasts, and supports a simple cart/checkout
flow. It exists to teach safe, scoped use of Cursor around UAT-protected
code — it is not a real client system.

## Coding Standards
- Python 3.11, PEP 8, type hints on all new public functions.
- Docstrings (Google style) required on every new public function/class.
- No bare `except:` — always catch a specific exception.
- Currency values always pass through `shared_utils.round_currency`.
- New modules go in `app/`; new tests go in `tests/` with a matching filename
  (`app/foo.py` -> `tests/test_foo.py`).

## NEVER_MODIFY
- app/baseline_forecast.py
- app/data_ingestion.py
- app/shared_utils.py
- app/auth/session.py
- app/cart.py
- app/checkout.py
- app/payments.py

## Prompt Templates

### Template: "Add a new read-only analytics module"
Task: Create a new module `app/<name>.py` that reads from <existing module>
without modifying it.
Scope: Only create new file(s) under app/ and tests/. Do not edit any file
listed in NEVER_MODIFY above.
Constraint: Follow the Coding Standards section. Include type hints and a
docstring on every public function.
Output format: Full file contents for the new module, plus a matching test
file with at least 3 test cases (happy path, edge case, invalid input).

### Template: "Fix a specific bug without touching unrelated code"
Task: Fix the bug described below in <file>: <bug description>.
Scope: Only change the minimum lines needed inside <file>. Do not refactor
unrelated code in the same file.
Constraint: Do not change the function's public signature or return type.
Output format: A unified diff, plus one sentence explaining the root cause.
